# Environment variables

Copy to `.env.local` for local development. In Vercel, add the same keys under **Project → Settings → Environment Variables**.

## Required for public site

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
```

## Required for contact form + admin CMS (Supabase)

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
```

## Optional

```bash
# Webhook for contact form notifications (n8n, etc.)
N8N_CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Webhook to notify on a new workflow access request (n8n, etc.).
# Unset means no notification is sent; the request is still stored and shows up
# in the admin Access Requests inbox. No fallback: set this explicitly (it may
# point at the same URL as the contact hook) so requester details are never
# routed anywhere you did not choose.
N8N_WORKFLOW_ACCESS_WEBHOOK_URL=

# --- "Ask my case studies" demo (retrieval + grounded answer) ---
# The demo always renders. With no key it runs in *example mode*: retrieval is
# still computed live from the in-repo passage index, and a saved example
# question/answer is shown with the input disabled. Set both DEMO_ASK_ENABLED
# and DEMO_LLM_API_KEY to switch the answer step on — that step calls a paid
# model, so it spends real money.

# Master switch. Unset/0 = example mode (the default, costs nothing).
DEMO_ASK_ENABLED=

# Server-only model key. NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
DEMO_LLM_API_KEY=

# "anthropic" (default) or "openai-compatible".
DEMO_LLM_PROVIDER=

# Defaults: claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 (anthropic) / gpt-4o-mini (openai-compatible).
# Haiku is the default because the demo only restates retrieved passages.
DEMO_LLM_MODEL=

# Override the API host, e.g. a gateway or a self-hosted OpenAI-compatible
# server. Defaults: https://api.anthropic.com / https://api.openai.com
DEMO_LLM_BASE_URL=

# Anthropic only: output_config.effort. Default "low" (cheap, right for a
# short grounded answer). Use "none" to omit the field entirely — required for
# models older than Opus 4.5, which reject it.
DEMO_LLM_EFFORT=

# Hard cap on answer tokens. Default 700. Raise it if you point
# DEMO_LLM_MODEL at a thinking model and answers come back truncated.
DEMO_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=

# Global ceiling on model calls per UTC day, per server instance. Default 100.
# Exceeding it fails closed with a friendly message — it never silently spends.
DEMO_DAILY_LIMIT=

# Retrieval method: "lexical" (default — BM25 keyword scoring, zero cost, no
# network) or "vector". "vector" needs an embeddings endpoint below; without
# one it falls back to lexical rather than mislabelling itself in the UI.
DEMO_RETRIEVER=

# Vector path only. OpenAI-compatible /v1/embeddings shape.
DEMO_EMBEDDINGS_API_KEY=
DEMO_EMBEDDINGS_URL=
DEMO_EMBEDDING_MODEL=

# Only needed for local database setup scripts
SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=
```

## Notes

- The portfolio renders with seed content when Supabase is not configured.
- Contact form and admin login require Supabase.
- Never expose `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` or `DEMO_LLM_API_KEY` as a `NEXT_PUBLIC_` variable.
- The "Ask my case studies" demo is disabled by default and degrades to a clearly labelled saved example, so leaving its variables blank is a supported state.
- Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` to your production domain before deploying (e.g. `https://abdullahdilshad.com`).

See `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` for the full Vercel deployment checklist.
